          <Pad Id="NFApfPqEKbd3SWOkm9xz6I" Comment="Title" Bounds="182,586,240,19" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="HowTo Play a Video with VL.Audio">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="CoreLibBasics.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="1lZWqM4vaWg7Gt2Tj22xHM" Bounds="85,680,830,172" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Notes:&#xD;&#xA;- Same picture as Video [Qt], but the sound only comes out at Audio; Qt's own audio output stays off. Windows only.&#xD;&#xA;- The sound follows the picture. Target: below 5 ms internally, about one video frame end to end.&#xD;&#xA;- Strict frame accuracy cannot be guaranteed with Qt's player; Sync Error shows the measured offset in ms.&#xD;&#xA;- Audio Offset (ms, optional pin, default 0) calibrates display and audio device latency: positive = the sound comes later.&#xD;&#xA;- Rate other than 1 plays like tape: the pitch changes with the rate, and a rate change may glitch once.&#xD;&#xA;- Volume (0..1) scales the signal at Audio. Sync Error is NaN while the sound locks in (start, jump, pause).&#xD;&#xA;- Path is relative to this patch.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="CoreLibBasics.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
